content:
Compared to iterative magnitude pruning (IMP) applied with the same pruning schedule (10 rounds, 20% pruning per round) and same training hyperparameters (SGD, learning rate 3e-4, momentum 0.9) but without reconstruction loss, on a ResNet50 backbone pretrained on ImageNet and transferred to COCO, the proposed method yields higher mAP at all reported structured sparsities. Specifically, mAP values (detection / segmentation) at each sparsity are:
      - 79.02%: IMP 32.1 / 29.9 vs proposed 32.7 / 30.3;
      - 83.22%: IMP 31.8 / 29.6 vs proposed 32.3 / 29.8;
      - 86.57%: IMP 31.3 / 29.1 vs proposed 31.6 / 29.5;
      - 89.26%: IMP 30.8 / 28.7 vs proposed 31.4 / 29.2;
      - 91.41%: IMP 30.1 / 28.0 vs proposed 30.5 / 28.4.
